# Benchmark build artifacts — regenerated by crisp-compile / crisp-hoist-cuda on every run.
# Do not check these in.
#
# ORDER MATTERS HERE.  Git applies the LAST matching rule, so this file is arranged in three
# blocks: artifacts, then a blanket re-include of source extensions, then the generated-harness
# rule which must come after that re-include in order to win.  Two mistakes were made here on
# 2026-08-25 and are called out so they are not repeated:
#   * `onemkl_*` / `sycl_control*` were written to catch compiled contender binaries, but they also
#     match onemkl_bf16.cpp, sycl_control.cpp and friends, which are SOURCE.  Hence the `!*.cpp`
#     block below.
#   * `*_L0.cpp` catches the generated per-kernel harnesses, but ALSO the hand-written fixtures
#     `matmul/crisp/bench_harness_l0.cpp` and `reduction/crisp/bench_harness_l0.cpp`, which are
#     source and must stay tracked.  Hence the explicit negations at the end.

# ---- 1. Artifacts -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hoist byproducts (metadata).
*.metacrisp

# Compiled kernels (.ptx / .spv) are regenerable too — but a fallback may be committed for
# machines where crisp-compile is absent, and is re-included by exception below:
#   bench-intel-driver.py  ships the .spv into the oneAPI Docker container
*.ptx
*.spv
!reduction/crisp/sum-reduce.spv

# Compiled benchmark binaries.  These were tracked by accident until 2026-08-25; native
# executables do not belong in source control.  The patterns are extension-free on purpose —
# the `!*.cpp` block below rescues the same-named sources.
*_bench_l0
matmul_crisp_l0
sycl_apples
sycl_control*
sycl_tla_peer
onemkl_*
cuda_apples
cublas_*
cutlass_peer
bin_*

# ---- 2. Source is never an artifact -------------------------------------------------------
!*.cpp
!*.cu
!*.crisp
!*.md
!*.py
!*.hpp
!*.h

# ---- 3. Generated per-kernel harnesses ----------------------------------------------------
# Must come AFTER the re-include above, or `!*.cpp` / `!*.cu` would rescue them too.
# `--hoist=l0` / `--hoist=cuda` emit one of these per kernel per sweep; they churn constantly.
*_L0.cpp
*_CUDA.cu

# The HAND-WRITTEN fixture harnesses are source, and their lowercase `_l0` would otherwise be
# caught by `*_L0.cpp` on a case-insensitive checkout (which Windows is by default).
!matmul/crisp/bench_harness_l0.cpp
!reduction/crisp/bench_harness_l0.cpp
